  subgraph I["🍰 PART I — BAKES PORTION MODEL ✅ APPROVED (Tina 6 Jul) — BUILD IT"]
    I0["RESEARCH (6 Jul): cake slice = 1 portion ≈ 100-115g (~350 kcal); round cake ≈ 10-14 slices (8in serves ~12) → slice ≈ 1/12. Biscuits = 2-3 small / 1-2 large ≈ 30-40g. Rolls/muffins/scones = 1 item = 1 portion."]
    I1["MODEL (yield-based). BATCH LAW (Tina): every bake = a fixed sensible batch, NEVER scale below one — no half cake, no 4 amaretti, no 2 rusks; dial rounds UP to whole batches; below one it stays at one (card notes keeps/freezes); each card states 'makes ~N'. (1) COUNTABLE SINGLES 1 item=1 person (rolls/muffins/scones/cupcakes/vetkoek/koeksisters/doughnuts) — yield 'makes 12'. (2) SLICEABLE 1 slice=1 portion (cakes/cheesecakes/tarts/loaves/dish-puddings) — serves-N: cake 12 · tart 8-10 · loaf 10. (3) BATCH TREATS like a cake (biscuits/cookies/rusks) — makes-~N by SIZE: small/amaretti ~40 · medium ~30 · large ~18 · rusks ~40 (derive from dough wt ÷ per-piece 15-45g); portion 2-3 small / 1-2 large / 1-2 rusks. (4) SPOONABLE ~150-200g (panna cotta/trifle). (5) LOAVES per slice (locked)."]
    I2["RESOLVED (Tina + Claude): dial stays PEOPLE everywhere (one shared qtyBox, no separate 'cakes' control), but bakes ANSWER in whole units — cake defaults to natural yield ('1 cake · serves 12 · 1 slice each'); step up rounds to whole cakes/batches ('20 → 2 cakes · serves 24'); display = per cake/slice/roll/batch; cost + Plan + shopping still aggregate by headcount. NEVER a fraction. ✅ DEFAULTS APPROVED (Tina 6 Jul): cake 12 · tart 8-10 · loaf 10 · cheesecake 12 · biscuits small ~40/med ~30/large ~18 · rusks ~40 (per-card override allowed). BUILD NOW — wire into bakes qtyBox."]
